# API Endpoint Rules

## RESTful Endpoints

### Properties
```
GET /api/properties - List all properties
GET /api/properties/{id} - Get property details
POST /api/properties - Create new property
PUT /api/properties/{id} - Update property
DELETE /api/properties/{id} - Delete property (soft delete)
```

### Tenants
```
GET /api/tenants - List all tenants
GET /api/tenants/{id} - Get tenant details
POST /api/tenants - Create new tenant
PUT /api/tenants/{id} - Update tenant
DELETE /api/tenants/{id} - Delete tenant (soft delete)
```

### Eviction Cases
```
GET /api/cases - List all cases
GET /api/cases/{id} - Get case details
POST /api/cases - Create new case
PUT /api/cases/{id} - Update case
DELETE /api/cases/{id} - Delete case (soft delete)

GET /api/cases/reports - Generate eviction reports
GET /api/cases/statistics - Get eviction statistics
```

## Request/Response Format
- Use consistent JSON structure
- Include pagination for list endpoints
- Implement proper error responses
- Follow HTTP status codes

## Authentication
- Require API key/token
- Implement rate limiting
- Use HTTPS only
- Log all API access

## Validation
- Validate all input data
- Sanitize user input
- Check permissions
- Verify data integrity

## Documentation
- Use OpenAPI/Swagger
- Include example requests
- Document error codes
- Provide SDK examples

## Performance
- Cache responses
- Optimize queries
- Compress responses
- Monitor response times

## Security
- Implement CORS
- Use API versioning
- Validate content types
- Prevent SQL injection

## Error Handling
```json
{
    "error": {
        "code": "ERROR_CODE",
        "message": "Human readable message",
        "details": {
            "field": "Additional error context"
        }
    }
}
```

## Response Format
```json
{
    "data": {
        // Response data
    },
    "meta": {
        "page": 1,
        "per_page": 10,
        "total": 100
    }
}
```

## Route Structure
```python
@app.route('/calculate', methods=['POST'])
@login_required
def calculate_timeline():
    """Calculate eviction timeline based on provided dates"""
    # Validate input
    validate_request_data(request.form)
    
    # Process calculation
    result = process_timeline_calculation(request.form)
    
    # Return response
    return jsonify(result)
```

## Authentication
- Require authentication for sensitive endpoints
- Use proper session management
- Implement rate limiting
- Log authentication attempts

## Input Validation
- Validate all input parameters
- Sanitize user input
- Check date formats
- Validate file uploads

## Response Format
```json
{
    "status": "success",
    "data": {
        "filing_date": "2025-04-08",
        "estimated_judgment_date": "2025-05-08",
        "days_remaining": 30
    },
    "message": "Timeline calculated successfully"
}
```

## Error Handling
- Use appropriate HTTP status codes
- Provide detailed error messages
- Handle all edge cases
- Log errors properly

## Security Guidelines
- Use HTTPS for all endpoints
- Implement CSRF protection
- Validate content types
- Sanitize file uploads

## Rate Limiting
- Implement per-user limits
- Set appropriate timeouts
- Monitor API usage
- Handle rate limit errors

## Documentation
- Document all endpoints
- Include request/response examples
- List required parameters
- Describe error responses 